What is what
------------

The icons hoja's own interface uses are Lucide, taken from lucide-static
1.26.0 and covered by the ISC licence above:

  arrow_left, arrow_right, arrow_up, check, chevron_down, chevron_up,
  house, magnifying_glass (Lucide's `search`), menu, pause, play,
  warning (Lucide's `triangle-alert`)

Two are renamed to the name hoja refers to them by; the file contents are
unmodified.

Everything else here is Zed's file-type icon set, reached through the
`file_icons` crate rather than by name. Those are 16x16 and drawn on their
own grid, and some of them are Lucide-derived in turn.

A large part of that set is brand and language marks — the Go gopher, the
Docker whale, the Rust logo, and so on. Those belong to their respective
projects and are used here as file-type icons under whatever terms each
project sets. They are not Lucide's, not Zed's, and not covered by the ISC
licence above.
